- Inventory days = year-end current inventory / reported cost of sales excluding DD&A × 365. Noncurrent inventory is excluded.
- Depreciation / PP&E = depreciation expense / opening net PP&E. The depreciation amounts are 43.998, 63.558, and 69.587; opening PP&E is 935.743, 1,158.054, and 1,251.496.
- Capital spending is cash additions to PP&E, shown as positive spending. The data-provider comparison remains unresolved.
- Effective tax rate = tax expense / pretax income. Tax benefits and pretax losses are both negative in 2024 and 2025.
- Reported growth = current revenue / prior-year revenue − 1. The 2023 calculation uses 2022 revenue of 527.510.

