## Forecast Assumptions

Five-year lists run from 2026 through 2030.

| Assumption | Value | Label | Reason |
|---|---|---|---|
| Revenue growth | 10% annually | judgment | Round the latest reported growth of 10.10%. NdPr volume growth is not the same as total revenue growth. |
| Gross margin proxy | 14.10% before DD&A | judgment | Use 2025 revenue minus reported cost of sales: (224.441 − 192.789) / 224.441. This is not confirmed reported gross margin. |
| SG&A | 354.06% of the pre-DD&A profit proxy | judgment | Preserve the 2025 relationship: 112.066 / (224.441 − 192.789). |
| Inventory days | 325 days | judgment | Round the latest historical ratio of 324.8 days. |
| Depreciation / opening net PP&E | 5.56% | judgment | Retain the latest historical ratio. |
| Capital spending | 550 in 2026; 206.897 annually in 2027–2030 | judgment | Use the 2026 guidance midpoint, then the three-year historical average. Assume no government-award receipts. |
| Tax rate | 28% on positive pretax income; zero on losses | judgment | Approximately the historical average, without assuming tax refunds. |
| NdPr sales volume | 2,500; 3,000; 3,500; 4,000; 4,500 metric tons | judgment | Add roughly 500 tons annually rather than repeat early-stage percentage growth. |
| Floor-plan financing | None / zero — not applicable | judgment | ABG's dealership financing structure does not apply to MP. |

Management guidance: the 2025 10-K states that 2026 capital costs are expected to be **500–600 million, net of government-award proceeds** (mp-10k2026.pdf, PDF p. 100). This is guidance for 2026 only; the later-year spending assumption is judgment.

## Company-Specific Line

**NdPr sales volume replaces ABG's same-store growth concept.** MP's expansion depends on selling more separated rare-earth material used in magnets, rather than increasing sales at existing stores. Volume helps explain growth, but prices and other products also affect total revenue.

